1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,513
CHAIRPERSON:

2
00:00:02,513 --> 00:00:02,694
Right.

3
00:00:02,694 --> 00:00:06,515
Next on the agenda we have traffic and highways.

4
00:00:06,515 --> 00:00:07,700
Councillor Thornton.

5
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:08,374
COUNCILLOR THORNTON:

6
00:00:08,374 --> 00:00:09,049
Thank you.

7
00:00:09,049 --> 00:00:14,107
Well, we now have the results of the survey carried out last month about traffic

8
00:00:14,107 --> 00:00:16,130
and road transport in the town.

9
00:00:16,130 --> 00:00:19,830
People were generally satisfied with the state of the roads.

10
00:00:19,830 --> 00:00:24,386
There were one or two complaints about potholes which will be addressed,

11
00:00:24,386 --> 00:00:29,702
but a significant number of people complained about the increasing number of heavy vehicles

12
00:00:29,702 --> 00:00:32,740
using our local roads to avoid traffic elsewhere.

13
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:37,686
We'd expected more complaints by commuters about the reduction in the train service,

14
00:00:37,686 --> 00:00:41,490
but it doesn't seem to have affected people too much.

15
00:00:41,490 --> 00:00:47,156
The cycle path that runs alongside the river is very well used by both cyclists

16
00:00:47,156 --> 00:00:50,555
and pedestrians since the surface was improved last year,

17
00:00:50,555 --> 00:00:55,844
but overtaking can be a problem so we're going to add a bit on

18
00:00:55,844 --> 00:00:58,110
the side to make it wider.

19
00:00:58,110 --> 00:01:02,475
At some stage, we'd like to extend the path so that it goes all

20
00:01:02,475 --> 00:01:04,034
the way through the town,

21
00:01:04,034 --> 00:01:06,840
but that won't be happening in the immediate future.

22
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:12,061
The plans to have a pedestrian crossing next to the Post Office have unfortunately

23
00:01:12,061 --> 00:01:15,790
had to be put on hold for the time being.

24
00:01:15,790 --> 00:01:18,773
We'd budgeted for this to be done this financial year,

25
00:01:18,773 --> 00:01:22,651
but then there were rumours that the Post Office was going to move,

26
00:01:22,651 --> 00:01:26,230
which would have meant there wasn't really a need for a crossing.

27
00:01:26,230 --> 00:01:29,108
Now they've confirmed that they're staying where they are,

28
00:01:29,108 --> 00:01:33,584
but the Highways Department have told us that it would be dangerous to have

29
00:01:33,584 --> 00:01:38,061
a pedestrian crossing where we'd originally planned it as there's a bend in the

30
00:01:38,061 --> 00:01:38,700
road there.

31
00:01:38,700 --> 00:01:40,820
So that'll need some more thought.

32
00:01:40,820 --> 00:01:46,026
On Station Road near the station and level crossing, drivers can face quite long

33
00:01:46,026 --> 00:01:48,258
waits if the level crossing's closed,

34
00:01:48,258 --> 00:01:53,464
and we've now got signs up requesting them not to leave their engines running

35
00:01:53,464 --> 00:01:54,580
at that time.

36
00:01:54,580 --> 00:01:59,701
This means pedestrians waiting on the pavement to cross he railway line don't have

37
00:01:59,701 --> 00:02:01,530
to breathe in car fumes.

38
00:02:01,530 --> 00:02:07,783
We've had some problems with cyclists leaving their bikes chained to the railings outside

39
00:02:07,783 --> 00:02:09,123
the ticket office,

40
00:02:09,123 --> 00:02:13,590
but the station has agreed to provide bike racks there.

41
00:02:13,590 --> 00:02:14,068
CHAIRPERSON:

42
00:02:14,068 --> 00:02:20,280
So next on the agenda is ‘Proposals for improvements to the recreation ground'.

43
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:22,070
Councillor Thornton again.

44
00:02:22,070 --> 00:02:22,749
COUNCILLOR THORNTON:

45
00:02:22,749 --> 00:02:27,505
Well, since we managed to extend the recreation ground, we've spent some time talking

46
00:02:27,505 --> 00:02:31,581
to local people about how it could be made a more attractive

47
00:02:31,581 --> 00:02:32,600
and useful space.

48
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:36,538
If you have a look at the map up on the screen, you can

49
00:02:36,538 --> 00:02:38,507
see the river up in the north,

50
00:02:38,507 --> 00:02:41,320
and the Community Hall near the entrance from the road.

51
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:46,240
At present, cars can park between the Community Hall and that line of trees

52
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:47,294
to the east,

53
00:02:47,294 --> 00:02:52,213
but this is quite dangerous for pedestrians so we're suggesting a new car park

54
00:02:52,213 --> 00:02:56,430
on the opposite side of the Community Hall, right next to it.

55
00:02:56,430 --> 00:03:00,170
We also have a new location for the cricket pitch.

56
00:03:00,170 --> 00:03:05,176
As we've now purchased additional space to the east of the recreation ground, beyond

57
00:03:05,176 --> 00:03:09,467
the trees, we plan to move it away from its current location,

58
00:03:09,467 --> 00:03:14,472
which is rather near the road, into this new area beyond the line of

59
00:03:14,472 --> 00:03:14,830
trees.

60
00:03:14,830 --> 00:03:20,040
This means there's less danger of stray balls hitting cars or pedestrians.

61
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:26,302
We've got plans for a children's playground which will be accessible by a footpath from the Community Hall

62
00:03:26,302 --> 00:03:28,390
and will be alongside the river.

63
00:03:28,390 --> 00:03:31,550
We'd originally thought of having it close to the road,

64
00:03:31,550 --> 00:03:34,710
but we think this will be a more attractive location.

65
00:03:34,710 --> 00:03:39,531
The skateboard ramp is very popular with both younger and older children – we

66
00:03:39,531 --> 00:03:42,497
had considered moving this up towards the river,

67
00:03:42,497 --> 00:03:47,688
but in the end we decided to have it in the southeast corner near

68
00:03:47,688 --> 00:03:48,430
the road.

69
00:03:48,430 --> 00:03:54,420
The pavilion is very well used at present by both football players and cricketers.

70
00:03:54,420 --> 00:03:58,695
It will stay where it is now – to the left of the line of trees

71
00:03:58,695 --> 00:04:02,400
and near to the river – handy for both the football and cricket pitches.

72
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:07,040
And finally, we'll be getting a new notice board for local information,

73
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:12,453
and that will be directly on people's right as they go from the road

74
00:04:12,453 --> 00:04:14,000
into the recreation ground.
